        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ചുമത്തുക",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ചുമത്തുക — cumattuka — \"to impose; to levy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സർക്കാർ പെട്രോളിന് പുതിയ നികുതി ചുമത്തി. sarkkār peṭrōḷinŭ putiya nikuti cumatti. The government imposed a new tax on petrol."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past: ചുമത്തി, cumatti."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also to bring a charge: കുറ്റം ചുമത്തുക (cumattuka), to charge with a crime."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ചുമത്തുക (cumattuka) is native Dravidian: DEDR 2677 lists Malayalam cumattuka, \"to load, to charge\", beside cuma, \"a burden\": to load a burden on someone."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
